      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fairmount was laid out in 1850, named after Philadelphia's Fairmount Park, and incorporated in 1870.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairmount%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "After a 1887 natural gas discovery, Fairmount became a glass‑industry hub during the Indiana Gas Boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairmount%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fairmount is the boyhood home of actor James Dean, who graduated high school in 1949 and is buried in the town’s Park Cemetery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairmount%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Fairmount Historical Museum, also called the James Dean Museum, displays 1950s memorabilia and features a “Cool Cat” Garfield statue.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.grantcounty.com/news/spotlight-on-fairmount-indiana-a-small-town-with-a-big-heart"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The James Dean Memorial Stage, once part of the high‑school auditorium, now hosts live bands from classic rock to country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.grantcounty.com/news/spotlight-on-fairmount-indiana-a-small-town-with-a-big-heart"
    },
